            {
              "id": "dbfd03ad-1996-4cc0-90eb-c98f41025c96",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "html": "<em><strong>Rhetoric/Composition/Play through Video Games: Reshaping Theory &amp; Practice of Writing </strong></em>is a collection of essays edited by Richard Colby &amp; Matthew Johnson, published by Palgrave Macmillan, March 20, 2013."
            },
            {
              "id": "38f0c97a-7a30-41d9-b064-670ceb4359da",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "html": ""
            },
            {
              "id": "d676b0ae-195c-47c7-a2e3-06528bc49233",
              "type": "quote",
              "html": "<em>An edited collection whose contributors analyze the relationship between writing, learning, and video games/videogaming, these essays consist of academic essays from writing and rhetoric teacher-scholars, who theorize, and contextualize how computer/video games enrich writing practices within and beyond the classroom and the teaching of writing.</em>"
            },
            {
              "id": "7b3674e8-6c46-42f7-a031-3fa360e448a5",
              "type": "paragraph",
